Falsifies `system_tests::user::terminal_swap_tests::a_hung_terminal_is_noticed_within_the_bound_and_replaced_without_its_state`.

Architecture: aarch64

The patch arms `terminal_supervisor`'s quiesce timer at four times `QUIESCE_BOUND_MS`, so the
supervisor still notices the hang and still replaces the terminal, only late. Every other assertion
in the test would pass; the one on how long the supervisor waited is what catches a bound that is
not the declared one.

Expected to fail: "the supervisor waited 1004 ms, against a bound of 250 ms" in the test's wait
assertion. Replayed red at exactly that assertion on aarch64 on 2026-10-19 (UTC).

diff --git a/components/src/terminal_supervisor.rs b/components/src/terminal_supervisor.rs
index 4f0852d2a..ec9fd4d9e 100644
--- a/components/src/terminal_supervisor.rs
+++ b/components/src/terminal_supervisor.rs
@@ -671,7 +671,7 @@ impl Supervisor<'_> {
         let bound = cntfrq() * s::QUIESCE_BOUND_MS / 1000;
         let started = now();
         if !process_builder::start_child(child, MODE_STAND_IN, 0, 0)
-            || timer_arm(d.timer, started + bound, d.wake, DEADLINE) < 0
+            || timer_arm(d.timer, started + 4 * bound, d.wake, DEADLINE) < 0
         {
             fail()
         }
